{"id":"d14f72c7fe1316ae9d186f1eed554e8099dba705","axis":"silent","repo":"vllm-project/vllm","sha":"d14f72c7fe1316ae9d186f1eed554e8099dba705","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"recipes/models/zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash.yaml","lines":["@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@ meta:","   provider: \"GLM (Z-AI)\"","   description: \"GLM-5.3-Flash is a 320B-total / 18B-active multimodal MoE with hybrid KDA and sparse MLA attention, native FP8 weights, MTP, and a 1M-token context window.\"","   date_added: 2026-08-27","-  date_updated: 2026-10-08","+  date_updated: 2026-10-19","   tasks:","     - text","     - multimodal","@@ -20,17 +20,21 @@ model:","   model_id: \"zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash\"","   min_vllm_version: \"0.29.0\"","   nightly_required: true","+  default_frontend: rust","   docker_image:","     nvidia: \"vllm/vllm-openai:nightly\"","     amd: \"vllm/vllm-openai-rocm:nightly\"","   install:","     docker:","-      note: \"NVIDIA: use vllm/vllm-openai:glm53-flash until support lands in the standard image. AMD: use the official vllm/vllm-openai-rocm:nightly image, which includes merged GLM-5.3-Flash support. Ascend 950PR: pin quay.io/ascend/vllm-ascend:nightly-main-a5 (same as GLM-5.3) with GLM-5.3-Flash overlays vLLM#53906 and vllm-ascend#15127.\"","+      note: \"Native GLM5Next rendering requires an image containing vllm-project/vllm#62424, including its Rust binary. Use NVIDIA/ROCm nightly images only once they include this change. Ascend 950PR also requires the nightly-main-a5 platform support and GLM-5.3-Flash overlays vLLM#53906 and vllm-ascend#15127.\"","     pip: false","   architecture: moe","   parameter_count: \"321B\"","   active_parameters: \"18B\"","   context_length: 1048576","+  base_args:","+    - \"--tokenizer-mode\"","+    - \"glm5_next\"","   base_env:","     VLLM_ENGINE_READY_TIMEOUT_S: \"3600\""," ","@@ -219,7 +223,7 @@ guide: |"," ","   - **Weights:** about 306 GiB for the default native FP8 checkpoint before runtime","     and KV-cache overhead; the BF16 variant requires roughly twice the weight memory","-  - **vLLM:** use docker before the integration is included in the public repo","+  - **vLLM:** an image containing [native GLM5Next support (#62424)](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/62424), including the matching Rust frontend binary. Older images need an updated build for the commands below.","   - **FlashInfer:** 0.6.17 or newer is required for NoPE sparse MLA"," ","   The default model ID, `zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash`, is the FP8 checkpoint. Select the BF16","@@ -227,12 +231,26 @@ guide: |","   `RedHatAI/GLM-5.3-Flash-NVFP4`. Its MoE experts are quantized to 4-bit (NVFP4),","   and it requires NVIDIA Blackwell GPUs."," ","+  ## Frontends","+","+  The command builder defaults to **Rust** and adds `--tokenizer-mode glm5_next`.","+  With `VLLM_USE_RUST_FRONTEND=1`, this selects native GLM5Next chat rendering for","+  the GLM-5.3-Flash template, including tool calls and reasoning options. Image and","+  video inputs are not yet supported on the Rust frontend; use the Python frontend","+  for multimodal requests.","+","+  Select **Python** in the command builder, or set `VLLM_USE_RUST_FRONTEND=0`,","+  to use the Hugging Face renderer and processor on the same build. On older builds","+  that do not recognize `glm5_next`, also replace `--tokenizer-mode glm5_next` with","+  `--tokenizer-mode auto`.","+","   ## Launching the server"," ","   ### FP8 with TP4 and MTP on one GB200 tray"," ","   ```bash","-  vllm serve zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash \\","+  VLLM_USE_RUST_FRONTEND=1 vllm serve zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash \\","+    --tokenizer-mode glm5_next \\","     --tensor-parallel-size 4 \\","     --kv-cache-dtype fp8 \\","     --speculative-config '{\"method\":\"mtp\",\"num_speculative_tokens\":5}' \\","@@ -259,7 +277,9 @@ guide: |","   VLLM_KV_CACHE_LAYOUT=HND \\","   UCX_NET_DEVICES=all \\","   VLLM_NIXL_SIDE_CHANNEL_PORT=5557 \\","+  VLLM_USE_RUST_FRONTEND=1 \\","   vllm serve zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash \\","+    --tokenizer-mode glm5_next \\","     --port 8001 \\","     --tensor-parallel-size 4 \\","     --kv-transfer-config '{\"kv_connector\":\"NixlConnector\",\"kv_role\":\"kv_producer\"}' \\","@@ -275,7 +295,9 @@ guide: |","   VLLM_KV_CACHE_LAYOUT=HND \\","   UCX_NET_DEVICES=all \\","   VLLM_NIXL_SIDE_CHANNEL_PORT=5558 \\","+  VLLM_USE_RUST_FRONTEND=1 \\","   vllm serve zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash \\","+    --tokenizer-mode glm5_next \\","     --port 8002 \\","     --tensor-parallel-size 4 \\","     --kv-transfer-config '{\"kv_connector\":\"NixlConnector\",\"kv_role\":\"kv_consumer\"}' \\","@@ -433,15 +455,16 @@ guide: |","   ","   ## Running on AMD Instinct"," ","-  Use the official `vllm/vllm-openai-rocm:nightly` image. GLM-5.3-Flash support","-  landed in [vLLM #53906](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/53906).","+  Use a `vllm/vllm-openai-rocm:nightly` build containing #62424 for native Rust","+  rendering. Model support landed in [vLLM #53906](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/53906)."," ","   ```bash","   export VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER=1","   # gfx950 (MI350X/MI355X) only","   export VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_FUSION_SHARED_EXPERTS=1","   export VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_TRITON_SPARSE_MLA=1","-  vllm serve zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash \\","+  VLLM_USE_RUST_FRONTEND=1 vllm serve zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash \\","+    --tokenizer-mode glm5_next \\","     --served-model-name zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash \\","     --tensor-parallel-size 4 \\","     --max-num-seqs 512 \\","@@ -466,7 +489,8 @@ guide: |","   (MI350X/MI355X), using the topk indexer backend from AITER is recommended:"," ","   ```bash","-  vllm serve zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash \\","+  VLLM_USE_RUST_FRONTEND=1 vllm serve zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash \\","+    --tokenizer-mode glm5_next \\","     --attention-backend ROCM_AITER_MLA_SPARSE \\","     --sparse-indexer-topk-backend aiter","   ```"],"additions":32,"deletions":8,"truncated":false},{"path":"recipes/models/zai-org/GLM-5.3.yaml","lines":["@@ -4,7 +4,7 @@ meta:","   provider: \"GLM (Z-AI)\"","   description: \"GLM-5.3 — Frontier Coding with Emergent Cyber Capabilities\"","   date_added: 2026-08-28","-  date_updated: 2026-10-15","+  date_updated: 2026-10-19","   tasks:","     - text","   performance_headline: \"Latest GLM-5 series MoE — native FP8 by default, 5-token MTP, 1M context\"","@@ -37,11 +37,18 @@ model:","   default_frontend: rust","   docker_image:","     amd: \"vllm/vllm-openai-rocm:v0.29.0\"","+  install:","+    pip:","+      note: \"Native GLM5Next rendering requires a build containing vllm-project/vllm#62424, including its Rust binary. The minimum version alone does not include this support.\"","+    docker:","+      note: \"Use an image containing vllm-project/vllm#62424, including its Rust binary. Older hardware-specific image pins require an updated build for --tokenizer-mode glm5_next.\"","   architecture: moe","   parameter_count: \"743B\"","   active_parameters: \"39B\"","   context_length: 1048576","   base_args:","+    - \"--tokenizer-mode\"","+    - \"glm5_next\"","     - \"--kv-cache-dtype\"","     - \"fp8_e4m3\"","   base_env: {}","@@ -255,32 +262,41 @@ guide: |","   ## Overview"," ","   **GLM-5.3** is the newest model in the GLM-5 series — a ~743B-parameter MoE (39B active) from **Z-AI**.","-  Architecture and serving flags are identical to GLM-5.2; the packaging change is that the","-  **default `zai-org/GLM-5.3` checkpoint is now native FP8** — BF16 weights live under the suffixed `zai-org/GLM-5.3-BF16` repo.","+  The **default `zai-org/GLM-5.3` checkpoint is native FP8** — BF16 weights live under the suffixed `zai-org/GLM-5.3-BF16` repo."," ","   The FP8 checkpoint fits on a single 8xH200 / 8xH20 node and — with FP8 KV cache — reaches the full 1M-token context on 8xB200.","   An NVFP4 checkpoint for Blackwell is published by Inferact (`Inferact/GLM-5.3-NVFP4`)."," ","   ## Prerequisites"," ","-  - **vLLM 0.28.0** or newer.","+  - **vLLM:** a build containing [native GLM5Next support (#62424)](https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/62424), including the matching Rust frontend binary.","+  - **Transformers:** 5.15.0 or newer.","   - **GPU:** 8xH200 or 8xH20 (141 GB each) for single-node FP8; 8xB200 (180 GB each) for the full 1M context."," ","   ## Installation"," ","-  ```bash","-  uv venv","-  source .venv/bin/activate","-  uv pip install \"vllm==0.28.0\" --torch-backend=auto","-  uv pip install \"transformers>=5.15.0\"","-  ```","+  Use a wheel or container built with #62424 for the Rust commands below.","+  The older release and hardware-specific image pins record prior model validation;","+  they need an updated build to use `--tokenizer-mode glm5_next`.","+","+  ## Frontends","+","+  The command builder defaults to **Rust** and adds `--tokenizer-mode glm5_next`.","+  With `VLLM_USE_RUST_FRONTEND=1`, this selects native GLM5Next chat rendering for","+  GLM-5.3, including tool calls and reasoning options.","+","+  Select **Python** in the command builder, or set `VLLM_USE_RUST_FRONTEND=0`,","+  to use the Hugging Face renderer on the same build. On older builds that do not","+  recognize `glm5_next`, also replace `--tokenizer-mode glm5_next` with","+  `--tokenizer-mode auto`."," ","   ## Launching the server"," ","   ### FP8 on 8xH200 (standard)"," ","   ```bash","-  vllm serve zai-org/GLM-5.3 \\","+  VLLM_USE_RUST_FRONTEND=1 vllm serve zai-org/GLM-5.3 \\","+    --tokenizer-mode glm5_next \\","     --kv-cache-dtype fp8 \\","     --tensor-parallel-size 8 \\","     --speculative-config.method mtp \\","@@ -296,7 +312,9 @@ guide: |","   ```bash","   VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER=1 \\","   VLLM_ROCM_USE_AITER_FUSION_SHARED_EXPERTS=1 \\","+  VLLM_USE_RUST_FRONTEND=1 \\","   vllm serve zai-org/GLM-5.3 \\","+    --tokenizer-mode glm5_next \\","     --kv-cache-dtype fp8_e4m3 \\","     --tensor-parallel-size 8 \\","     --speculative-config.method mtp \\","@@ -311,7 +329,7 @@ guide: |","     --moe-backend aiter","   ```"," ","-  On 8x MI325X with `vllm/vllm-openai-rocm:v0.29.0`, this command serves the full","+  Earlier validation on 8x MI325X with `vllm/vllm-openai-rocm:v0.29.0` served","   `--max-model-len 524288` at `--gpu-memory-utilization 0.80`, reporting a 1,477,168-token","   KV cache and 2.82x maximum concurrency. MTP is healthy there: a mean acceptance length of","   2.77 with 5 tokens drafted per step on a ~500-token greedy generation.","@@ -328,7 +346,8 @@ guide: |","   (`--kv-cache-dtype fp8_e4m3`, already in the base flags) roughly halves that budget."," ","   ```bash","-  vllm serve zai-org/GLM-5.3 \\","+  VLLM_USE_RUST_FRONTEND=1 vllm serve zai-org/GLM-5.3 \\","+    --tokenizer-mode glm5_next \\","     --kv-cache-dtype fp8_e4m3 \\","     --tensor-parallel-size 8 \\","     --speculative-config.method mtp \\","@@ -351,7 +370,8 @@ guide: |","   Select the **NVFP4** variant above (Blackwell-only) or run:"," ","   ```bash","-  vllm serve Inferact/GLM-5.3-NVFP4 \\","+  VLLM_USE_RUST_FRONTEND=1 vllm serve Inferact/GLM-5.3-NVFP4 \\","+    --tokenizer-mode glm5_next \\","     --tensor-parallel-size 8 \\","     --enable-expert-parallel \\","     --reasoning-parser glm47 \\","@@ -368,7 +388,8 @@ guide: |","   with eight speculative tokens:"," ","   ```bash","-  vllm serve zai-org/GLM-5.3 \\","+  VLLM_USE_RUST_FRONTEND=1 vllm serve zai-org/GLM-5.3 \\","+    --tokenizer-mode glm5_next \\","     --tensor-parallel-size 8 \\","     --speculative-config '{\"method\":\"dspark\",\"model\":\"RedHatAI/GLM-5.3-speculator.dspark\",\"num_speculative_tokens\":8}'","   ```"],"additions":36,"deletions":15,"truncated":false},{"path":"rust/src/chat/src/backend/hf.rs","lines":["@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@ use crate::parser::unified::{HfTemplateError, ResponseTemplate};"," use crate::renderer::hf::{HfChatRenderer, MultimodalRenderInfo};"," use crate::renderer::{","     DeepSeekV4ChatRenderer, DeepSeekV32ChatRenderer, DeepSeekV41ChatRenderer, DynChatRenderer,","-    HarmonyChatRenderer, InklingChatRenderer, KimiK3ChatRenderer,","+    Glm5NextChatRenderer, HarmonyChatRenderer, InklingChatRenderer, KimiK3ChatRenderer,"," };"," use crate::request::ChatRequest;"," use crate::{DynChatOutputProcessor, RendererSelection};","@@ -99,6 +99,11 @@ impl HfChatBackend {","                 tokenizer.clone(),","                 options.default_chat_template_kwargs,","             )),","+            RendererSelection::Glm5Next => Arc::new(","+                Glm5NextChatRenderer::new(options.default_chat_template_kwargs)","+                    .with_multimodal(model_type == \"glm5_next\")","+                    .with_tokenizer(tokenizer.clone())?,","+            ),","         };"," ","         info!("],"additions":6,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"rust/src/chat/src/renderer/glm5_next/encoding.rs","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,535 @@","+// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0","+// SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright contributors to the vLLM project","+","+use std::collections::{HashMap, HashSet};","+use std::fmt::Write as _;","+use std::io::{self, Write};","+","+use serde::Serialize;","+use serde_json::ser::{Formatter, Serializer};","+use serde_json::{Value, json};","+use thiserror_ext::AsReport as _;","+","+use super::writer::Glm5PromptWriter;","+use crate::error::{Error, Result, bail_chat_template_thrown, chat_template_thrown};","+use crate::renderer::MediaPartSource;","+use crate::request::{ChatContent, ChatContentPart, ChatMessage, ChatTool, GenerationPromptMode};","+use crate::{AssistantContentBlock, AssistantMessageExt};","+","+const TOOLS_PREFIX: &str = \"<|system|>\\n# Tools\\n\\nYou may call one or more functions to assist with the user query.\\n\\nYou are provided with function signatures within <tools></tools> XML tags:\\n<tools>\\n\";","+const TOOLS_SUFFIX: &str = \"</tools>\\n\\nFor each function call, output the function name and arguments within the following XML format:\\n<tool_call>{function-name}<arg_key>{arg-key-1}</arg_key><arg_value>{arg-value-1}</arg_value><arg_key>{arg-key-2}</arg_key><arg_value>{arg-value-2}</arg_value>...</tool_call>\";","+","+pub(super) fn truthy(value: &Value) -> bool {","+    match value {","+        Value::Null => false,","+        Value::Bool(value) => *value,","+        Value::Number(value) => value.as_f64() != Some(0.0),","+        Value::String(value) => !value.is_empty(),","+        Value::Array(value) => !value.is_empty(),","+        Value::Object(value) => !value.is_empty(),","+    }","+}","+","+fn text(value: &Value) -> String {","+    match value {","+        Value::Null => \"None\".into(),","+        Value::Bool(true) => \"True\".into(),","+        Value::Bool(false) => \"False\".into(),","+        Value::String(value) => value.clone(),","+        _ => value.to_string(),","+    }","+}","+","+#[derive(Default)]","+struct MediaContext {","+    enabled: bool,","+    order: Vec<MediaPartSource>,","+}","+","+fn visible_text(","+    out: &mut Glm5PromptWriter<'_>,","+    value: &Value,","+    media: &mut MediaContext,","+) -> Result<()> {","+    match value {","+        Value::Null => {}","+        Value::String(value) => out.ordinary(value),","+        Value::Array(parts) => {","+            for part in parts {","+                if let Some(part) = part.as_str() {","+                    out.ordinary(part);","+                    continue;","+                }","+                match part[\"type\"].as_str().unwrap_or_default() {","+                    \"text\" => out.ordinary(&part.get(\"text\").map(text).unwrap_or_default()),","+                    kind @ (\"image\" | \"image_url\" | \"video\" | \"video_url\" | \"audio\"","+                    | \"audio_url\" | \"input_audio\") => {","+                        let kind = kind.replace(\"_url\", \"\").replace(\"input_\", \"\");","+                        if media.enabled {","+                            out.control(&format!(\"<|begin_of_{kind}|>\"))?;","+                            if kind != \"audio\" {","+                                out.control(&format!(\"<|{kind}|>\"))?;","+                            }","+                            out.control(&format!(\"<|end_of_{kind}|>\"))?;","+                            if let (Some(message_index), Some(content_part_index)) = (","+                                part[\"message_index\"].as_u64(),","+                                part[\"content_part_index\"].as_u64(),","+                            ) {","+                                media.order.push(MediaPartSource {","+                                    message_index: message_index as usize,","+                                    content_part_index: content_part_index as usize,","+                                });","+                            }","+                        } else {","+                            out.control(&format!(\"<reminder>You are unable to process this {kind} because you don't have multi-modal input ability. Try different methods.</reminder>\"))?;","+                        }","+                    }","+                    _ => {}","+                }","+            }","+        }","+        _ => out.ordinary(&text(value)),","+    }","+    Ok(())","+}","+","+fn tool_definition(tool: &Value) -> Result<String> {","+    let Some(fields) = tool.as_object() else {","+        bail_chat_template_thrown!(\"Each tool must be a JSON object\");","+    };","+    let mut out = String::from(\"{\");","+    for (key, value) in fields {","+        if key == \"strict\" || key == \"defer_loading\" {","+            continue;","+        }","+        if out.len() > 1 {","+            out.push_str(\", \");","+        }","+        write!(out, \"\\\"{key}\\\": {}\", json(value)?).unwrap();","+    }","+    out.push('}');","+    Ok(out)","+}","+","+fn unwrap_tool(tool: &Value) -> &Value {","+    tool.get(\"function\").unwrap_or(tool)","+}","+","+fn tool_references(value: &Value) -> bool {","+    value","+        .as_array()","+        .and_then(|parts| parts.first())","+        .is_some_and(|part| part[\"type\"] == \"tool_reference\")","+}","+","+fn reference_response(out: &mut Glm5PromptWriter<'_>, refs: &Value, tools: &[Value]) -> Result<()> {","+    if tools.is_empty() {","+        bail_chat_template_thrown!(\"Rendering a tool_reference requires tools\");","+    }","+    out.control(\"<tool_response><tools>\\n\")?;","+    for reference in refs.as_array().into_iter().flatten() {","+        for tool in tools.iter().map(unwrap_tool) {","+            if tool.get(\"name\") == reference.get(\"name\") {","+                out.ordinary(&tool_definition(tool)?);","+                out.control(\"\\n\")?;","+            }","+        }","+    }","+    out.control(\"</tools></tool_response>\")","+}","+","+fn response(","+    out: &mut Glm5PromptWriter<'_>,","+    value: &Value,","+    tools: &[Value],","+    media: &mut MediaContext,","+) -> Result<()> {","+    if tool_references(value) {","+        reference_response(out, value, tools)","+    } else {","+        out.control(\"<tool_response>\")?;","+        visible_text(out, value, media)?;","+        out.control(\"</tool_response>\")","+    }","+}","+","+fn bundled_outputs(value: &Value) -> Result<bool> {","+    if !truthy(value) || value.is_string() {","+        return Ok(false);","+    }","+    let Some(parts) = value.as_array() else {","+        bail_chat_template_thrown!(\"A tool message content must be a string or a list\");","+    };","+    Ok(parts.first().is_some_and(|part| part.get(\"output\").is_some()))","+}","+","+fn tool_response(","+    out: &mut Glm5PromptWriter<'_>,","+    message: &Value,","+    tools: &[Value],","+    media: &mut MediaContext,","+) -> Result<()> {","+    let value = &message[\"content\"];","+    if tool_references(value) {","+        return reference_response(out, value, tools);","+    }","+    if bundled_outputs(value)? {","+        for part in value.as_array().unwrap() {","+            response(out, &part[\"output\"], tools, media)?;","+        }","+        Ok(())","+    } else {","+        response(out, value, tools, media)","+    }","+}","+","+fn id(value: &Value) -> String {","+    [\"tool_call_id\", \"id\"]","+        .into_iter()","+        .filter_map(|key| value.get(key))","+        .find(|value| truthy(value))","+        .map(text)","+        .unwrap_or_default()","+}","+","+fn ordered_tool_block(","+    out: &mut Glm5PromptWriter<'_>,","+    block: &[Value],","+    assistant: Option<&Value>,","+    tools: &[Value],","+    media: &mut MediaContext,","+) -> Result<()> {","+    let calls = assistant","+        .filter(|message| message[\"role\"] == \"assistant\")","+        .and_then(|message| message[\"tool_calls\"].as_array())","+        .filter(|calls| !calls.is_empty());","+    if let Some(calls) = calls {","+        let mut can_sort = true;","+        let mut responses = HashMap::new();","+        for message in block {","+            if bundled_outputs(&message[\"content\"])? {","+                for entry in message[\"content\"].as_array().unwrap() {","+                    let key = id(entry);","+                    if key.is_empty() || responses.insert(key, &entry[\"output\"]).is_some() {","+                        can_sort = false;","+                    }","+                }","+            } else {","+                let key = id(message);","+                if key.is_empty() || responses.insert(key, &message[\"content\"]).is_some() {","+                    can_sort = false;","+                }","+            }","+        }","+        let call_ids: Vec<_> = calls.iter().map(id).collect();","+        let mut seen = HashSet::new();","+        for key in &call_ids {","+            if key.is_empty() || !seen.insert(key) {","+                can_sort = false;","+            }","+        }","+        if can_sort && responses.keys().all(|key| seen.contains(key)) {","+            for value in call_ids.iter().filter_map(|key| responses.get(key)) {","+                response(out, value, tools, media)?;","+            }","+            return Ok(());","+        }","+    }","+    for message in block {","+        tool_response(out, message, tools, media)?;","+    }","+    Ok(())","+}","+","+fn tool_call(out: &mut Glm5PromptWriter<'_>, call: &Value) -> Result<()> {","+    let call = call.get(\"function\").filter(|value| truthy(value)).unwrap_or(call);","+    let Some(name) = call[\"name\"].as_str() else {","+        bail_chat_template_thrown!(\"Each tool_call needs a string name\");","+    };","+    let parsed;","+    let arguments = if let Some(raw) = call[\"arguments\"].as_str() {","+        parsed = serde_json::from_str::<Value>(raw).map_err(|error| {","+            chat_template_thrown!(\"Invalid tool_call arguments: {}\", error.as_report())","+        })?;","+        &parsed","+    } else {","+        &call[\"arguments\"]","+    };","+    let Some(arguments) = arguments.as_object() else {","+        bail_chat_template_thrown!(\"tool_call arguments must be a JSON object\");","+    };","+    out.control(\"<tool_call>\")?;","+    out.ordinary(name);","+    for (key, value) in arguments {","+        out.control(\"<arg_key>\")?;","+        out.ordinary(key);","+        out.control(\"</arg_key><arg_value>\")?;","+        if let Some(value) = value.as_str() {","+            out.ordinary(value);","+        } else {","+            out.ordinary(&json(value)?);","+        }","+        out.control(\"</arg_value>\")?;","+    }","+    out.control(\"</tool_call>\")","+}","+","+#[cfg(test)]","+pub(super) fn render(","+    messages: &[Value],","+    tools: &[Value],","+    mode: GenerationPromptMode,","+    kwargs: &HashMap<String, Value>,","+) -> Result<String> {","+    let mut out = Glm5PromptWriter::new(None);","+    render_into(&mut out, messages, tools, mode, kwargs, false)?;","+    Ok(out.text().to_owned())","+}","+","+/// Render into `out`, returning media parts in placeholder order.","+pub(super) fn render_into(","+    out: &mut Glm5PromptWriter<'_>,","+    messages: &[Value],","+    tools: &[Value],","+    mode: GenerationPromptMode,","+    kwargs: &HashMap<String, Value>,","+    multimodal: bool,","+) -> Result<Vec<MediaPartSourc